\caption{Per-layer $R^2$ action-probe profiles for three architectures, each comparing trained (solid) and untrained (dashed) checkpoints.
All VLM-to-VLA trained cells show significant peak-to-exit collapse ($\Delta R^2 = 0.16$--$0.36$; clustered bootstrap 95\% CI excludes zero), while untrained VLM baselines show flat profiles (all CIs include zero).
No OpenVLA (VLA-to-VLA) cell reaches significance ($\Delta R^2 = 0.03$--$0.12$; all CIs include zero); the OXE-pretrained baseline has already undergone exit-layer reorganization.}
